      "message": "I don\u0027t think startOffset can exist as a uint16. Weird programs \u003e64K are definitely possible. \n\nMy earlier suggestion was, store the length of the range as a uint16, and change IRNode::fKind to an uint16. So in this scenario `fEndOffset` would become `uint16 fLength`. We would need to make sure that fKind and fLength are next to each other (this seems to happen naturally). ",
